// ===== Singapore Changi Airport: passenger terminals T1-T4, piers, aerobridges and the apron (sites 'changiair', 'changit4') =====
// Built on the real OSM footprints (T1 1981 / 2012 facelift + 2019 extension and canopy to Jewel, T2 1990 / 2023 upgrade,
// T3 2008 with its skylight roof, T4 2017) in local metres round 1.3550 N 103.9890 E (+x east, +z south, y absolute).
// Jewel and the control tower are separate landmarks (lm16/sg2/changi.js): nothing here touches them.
//
// window.SG_STANDS — the aircraft stands, defined when this file loads (read by the aircraft / ground-vehicle module):
//   [{x, y, a, code, bridges, gate}, ...]   in WORLD metres (x east, y north = the sgXY frame)
//   (x, y)  where the NOSE of the parked aircraft stops (on the stand centre line)
//   a       nose heading in radians, math convention in the world x/y plane (0 = east, PI/2 = north); contact stands
//           point the nose at the terminal facade, remote stands at the apron edge (tail toward the taxilane)
//   code    'C' (A320 / 737, span <= 36 m), 'E' (777 / 787 / A350 / A330, <= 65 m), 'F' (A380 / 747-8, <= 80 m)
//   bridges 0 = remote stand (buses), 1, 2 or 3 aerobridges; every bridge serves a door on the aircraft's LEFT side:
//           C: L1 5 m aft of the nose, 2.0 m left of the centre line, sill 3.3 m
//           E: L1 7 m and L2 21 m aft, 3.1 m left, sill 4.8 m
//           F: M1 9 m and M2 22 m aft (sill 5.1 m), U1 upper deck 28 m aft (sill 7.9 m), 3.6 m left
